{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"The valid-path test will load each `.so` by absolute path, resolve `helloworld` from each library, redirect the process stdout at the file-descriptor boundary, and compare both return values and emitted bytes. Since there is no input domain to randomize, it will use a fixed-seed sequence of 64 randomized invocation counts to catch state or repeated-call differences without calling the Rust implementation directly."}}
